    {
      "key": "40cdf1a7-ef2a-424f-935b-3e0051934f41",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "40cdf1a7-ef2a-424f-935b-3e0051934f41",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1cfe6627-7acc-4733-ac0d-a93e32a27aa8"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e6dfda49-8748-48c9-b59a-54b55f967d2d",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students connect the die roll warm-up to the key vocabulary they will use when reading and writing programs with random values.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 28, Level 1. Have students read the code and predict what numbers the program might print before pressing Run.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Listen for students identifying 1 as the smallest possible value and 6 as the largest possible value. Encourage them to explain why the program should not print numbers outside that range.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Predict & Run",
        "progression_name": "Predict & Run",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Connect this level back to the die roll warm-up. randint(1, 6) works like rolling a six-sided die: it can choose whole numbers from 1 through 6, and both endpoints are included."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e6dfda49-8748-48c9-b59a-54b55f967d2d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2d5bc9f4-a7ff-4899-aaf3-8bd6698eb156",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What did you notice about the code in this program?*\n- *What do you wonder about the code in this program?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that the program uses randint() to choose a value from a set range. Listen for students wondering how the starting and ending values affect which numbers can be chosen."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2d5bc9f4-a7ff-4899-aaf3-8bd6698eb156",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "93f8db0f-44d4-49f8-8dd8-eb9701037e66",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Have students take out their copy of the CSP Unit 1 Unit Guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "93f8db0f-44d4-49f8-8dd8-eb9701037e66",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3adccbd9-3bac-4293-82e7-a1caa53e0d09",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *randint().*",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Emphasize that a and b stand for the starting and ending values. In randint(1, 6), the program can choose any whole number from 1 through 6."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3adccbd9-3bac-4293-82e7-a1caa53e0d09",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0fce11f3-0544-44ec-8b1b-47059f2a5c98",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *inclusive.* Use the image on the slide to provide an example: **randint(1,6)** includes 1 and 6.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Make sure students understand that the endpoints are included. In randint(1, 6), both 1 and 6 are possible results, just like rolling a die."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0fce11f3-0544-44ec-8b1b-47059f2a5c98",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "60ec8e60-1bc5-4fe3-9bb2-66453a0ff6bf",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students investigate how randint() creates random values in code by tracing a simple program, testing it multiple times, and explaining why the output can change each time it runs.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 28, Level 2. Have students run the code, trace what each line does, and add comments explaining how **randint(1, 6)** affects the output.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students explaining that randint(1, 6) stores a random number from 1 through 6 in the variable roll, and that print(roll) displays that value.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Investigate",
        "progression_name": "Investigate"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "60ec8e60-1bc5-4fe3-9bb2-66453a0ff6bf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f8cbcbbe-a622-4355-aa9f-215124c35415",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animated slide to explain the **import** line. Emphasize that Python needs this line to access the **randint()** command."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f8cbcbbe-a622-4355-aa9f-215124c35415",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c82954ff-5bc8-4719-acd4-6f03de80c824",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "**randint()** is not built into every Python program automatically. This import line gets **randint()** from the random module so we can use it in our code.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c82954ff-5bc8-4719-acd4-6f03de80c824",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "690bcd6e-5f80-4dea-97c8-55fb35f463bc",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animated slide to explain how random values are created and stored. Have students annotate the code snippet in their Unit Guide.\n- First, **randint()** chooses a random value within the range.\n- Then the variable stores that value.\n- Later, the program can use the variable in another command, like **print()** or **paint(red, green, blue)**."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "690bcd6e-5f80-4dea-97c8-55fb35f463bc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f6f7b7c4-e90e-4f7d-91c4-2ac69f3574ed",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students modify randint() ranges to create different random outcomes, then explain how the smallest and largest values affect what the program can generate.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 28, Level 3. Have students change the range to simulate a 20-sided die, test the program, then choose their own die size and explain the smallest and largest possible values.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students changing the second value in randint(1, 6) and testing the program multiple times. Check that students understand the first value is the smallest possible result and the second value is the largest possible result.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Modify",
        "progression_name": "Modify",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that changing the range changes the possible outputs. If they use **randint(1, 20)**, the program can choose any whole number from 1 through 20, including both endpoints."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f6f7b7c4-e90e-4f7d-91c4-2ac69f3574ed",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ff397e55-f714-4e9d-9d9d-fc231e87ffae",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** What did you discover from the modifications you made to the code?\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should explain that changing the values inside randint() changes the range of possible outputs. Listen for students to use words like smallest, largest, range, and inclusive."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ff397e55-f714-4e9d-9d9d-fc231e87ffae",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2379fc17-d2ae-41d0-a697-954b7c47cbd6",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 28, Level 4 to complete Levels 4 through 5.\n- **Level 4A:** Students add a second random die roll and calculate the total.\n- **Level 4B:** Students use custom low and high values inside **randint()**.\n- **Level 4C:** Students use **randint()** to generate random bonus points.\n- **Level 5:** Students respond to a free-response question about whether **randint(1, 20)** includes 1 and 20.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students using randint() in new contexts while keeping track of the possible range. Encourage them to test more than once and explain why the output changes.",
        "progression_name": "Modify and Extend",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Emphasize that **randint()** can be used for more than dice. It can generate random scores, bonuses, ranges, colors, positions, and other values as long as students choose reasonable minimum and maximum numbers."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use Level 5 to check whether students understand that randint(a, b) is inclusive, meaning both a and b can be chosen."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2379fc17-d2ae-41d0-a697-954b7c47cbd6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8b42512a-5f61-4d21-8eb9-d0e2b02ecec2",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Modify and Extend"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8b42512a-5f61-4d21-8eb9-d0e2b02ecec2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "09878874-bd42-424b-bfca-5730f8ef538c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1919050f-6ea9-4c4a-bb41-a2b3d2f4f5e2",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
