      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c1e8b430-8d21-41b7-854c-51171ba5aa37",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day and give students a moment to just think about what they learned today. Facilitate a pair-share with the class to share their thoughts on the question of the day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c1e8b430-8d21-41b7-854c-51171ba5aa37",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8fbdf855-53b6-4c5f-b1bc-5fb770a8468e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "79db2598-be73-4296-be21-6fdcd8112dae",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "79db2598-be73-4296-be21-6fdcd8112dae",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8fbdf855-53b6-4c5f-b1bc-5fb770a8468e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2886ef26-a567-4390-b7df-1d5d369bb9f7",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students identify which parts of a visual effect could be randomized and explain why randomization can improve the user experience.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *Which scene elements should be randomized to make this scene feel more natural, surprising, or fun for the user?*\n- *Which should remain consistent to maintain visual structure?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students to name specific elements like color, size, position, number of sparks, timing, and movement. Push them to explain the effect on the viewer, not just name what changes."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2886ef26-a567-4390-b7df-1d5d369bb9f7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94d61164-9d45-40f8-bde4-e1c606e46997"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8741727a-4fef-4231-a47c-a36dab7c4600",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through each layer of the slide to reveal one randomized element at a time: color, size, position, and other possibilities."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8741727a-4fef-4231-a47c-a36dab7c4600",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94d61164-9d45-40f8-bde4-e1c606e46997"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b705685e-0b3e-45ee-8802-c20ab2356ba3",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Randomization is not just making everything different. We choose specific parts of a scene to change so the scene feels more alive while still looking intentional. In Theater, you can randomize many parts of your scene, including color, size, position, movement, and even sounds. Today, you’ll use randint() during the Make step to control what changes in your own graphic.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b705685e-0b3e-45ee-8802-c20ab2356ba3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94d61164-9d45-40f8-bde4-e1c606e46997"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1220b35d-a9c0-401a-b247-3d74f16bde1c",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1220b35d-a9c0-401a-b247-3d74f16bde1c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94d61164-9d45-40f8-bde4-e1c606e46997"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2e3dc170-e3d8-4245-9494-1f9f7822f16a",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2e3dc170-e3d8-4245-9494-1f9f7822f16a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94d61164-9d45-40f8-bde4-e1c606e46997"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2130fe04-e6a7-44b1-80af-92279e9517e7",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students choose one existing Theater scene and use randint() to make one part of the scene change each time the program runs.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 29, Level 1. Students should choose one option:\n- **Level 1A**: Randomize the note that plays.\n- **Level 1B**: Randomize where an object appears.\n- **Level 1C**: Randomize the spotlight color.\n- **Level 1D**: Randomize multiple effects, such as color, position, or sound.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students storing random values in variables and then using those variables inside the Theater commands. Encourage them to run the program more than once so they can observe what changes.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Modify: Random Effects",
        "progression_name": "Modify: Random Effects",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that some effects have clear number ranges: RGB colors use 0–255, positions should stay within the canvas size, and MIDI notes should stay within the note range given in the prompt. Encourage students to start within those ranges, then narrow the minimum and maximum values if they want the random effect to look or sound more intentional."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2130fe04-e6a7-44b1-80af-92279e9517e7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3bf495c4-6415-4e4b-a7ce-f45d798d2142",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What did you randomize?*\n- *How did it change the user’s experience of your scene?*\n- *Did you adjust your number range? Why?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students to connect specific code choices to visual or sound effects, such as changing color, position, size, or notes. Ask them to explain how the randomization made the scene feel more natural, surprising, or intentional."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3bf495c4-6415-4e4b-a7ce-f45d798d2142",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f9858c0e-fa93-4e74-a81d-19b4e621b04a",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students plan and create their own Theater scene by first brainstorming the scene and its key elements, then using AI Tutor to build the scene and **randint()** to randomize at least two parts of it.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Random Scene activity guide.",
        "duration": "25",
        "name": "Random Scene"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f9858c0e-fa93-4e74-a81d-19b4e621b04a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "dd377c3f-e238-4b47-b806-8bf2f1e2dfe6",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to page 1 of the activity guide. Have them choose a scene idea, sketch their design, list the background, objects, and sounds they will need, and identify at least two values they may randomize.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students breaking their scene into clear parts before coding. Encourage them to name specific elements they can build in Theater, such as a background, objects, details, sounds, and random effects.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that this plan should help them code. Their sketch does not need to be perfect, but they should be able to explain what they want to create and which parts will change randomly."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "dd377c3f-e238-4b47-b806-8bf2f1e2dfe6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c2394b4e-24ac-45a2-908a-f9310939b19e",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to page 2 of the activity guide. Have them review the rubric before they begin coding."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c2394b4e-24ac-45a2-908a-f9310939b19e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "405c8d5e-8855-4367-b690-cf388e3c4319",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 29, Level 2. Have students use their sketch and plan as a guide while they code. Remind them to test often instead of waiting until the end.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students using AI Tutor to build a complete Theater scene, then adding randint() to randomize at least two values, such as color, position, size, or notes.",
        "progression_name": "Make: Random Effects",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this level to check whether students can apply randint() independently, choose appropriate number ranges, and explain what they randomized through comments in their code."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "405c8d5e-8855-4367-b690-cf388e3c4319",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32750681-4a65-4fc5-a6c7-0a7ab6b6fd0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "866be94f-b985-430d-b14a-dbce3c2cc7ef",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
