    {
      "key": "f52f527b-f6e0-4e5d-920f-5fea1d4e3db1",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to read the project rubric."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f52f527b-f6e0-4e5d-920f-5fea1d4e3db1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "148fa949-5ee6-4c6d-b7f7-3fc1be24cac5",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What do you notice about the project requirements and rubric?*\n- *What does success look like for this project?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students share what they notice about the project requirements and rubric and identify the components to implement in their program."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "148fa949-5ee6-4c6d-b7f7-3fc1be24cac5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "70b7368c-9df5-4e40-86c1-3752681ebc2e",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the milestone structure of the project. Explain that the Wrapped Project is divided into three milestones. Use the visual roadmap to preview the journey students will take: interviewing a real user and planning on Day 1, building their program and animated recap with AI support on Day 2, then testing, fixing, and reflecting on Day 3.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that milestones help them manage time and track progress, just like in real design and development projects. Encourage them to think of each milestone as a \"checkpoint\" to reflect on what's working, what needs improvement, and how their design aligns with their user and purpose."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "70b7368c-9df5-4e40-86c1-3752681ebc2e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5641334b-7083-4652-a038-bf427ce359d2",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students draft interview questions designed to surface real numeric data, then check those questions for hidden assumptions before using them on a real person — practicing bias awareness at the design stage, before any code or output exists.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students individually write 3–4 questions they'll ask their partner. At least one question should be designed to produce a number.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Ask Good Questions",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students write a question that can only be answered with a fact, not a number (e.g. \"What's your favorite team?\"), have them add a follow-up that quantifies it (e.g. \"How many games have you been to this season?\")."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5641334b-7083-4652-a038-bf427ce359d2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "45446bc1-cd4f-4bb1-9bff-59bd99201a89",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have partners trade their drafted questions and check each other's for built-in assumptions. Have them revise anything flagged before moving on.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Listen for students catching real assumptions, not just politeness edits.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this activity to check whether students can identify an assumption embedded in a question and explain what's biased about it, not just that something feels off."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "45446bc1-cd4f-4bb1-9bff-59bd99201a89",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cf4fa80a-ad93-42da-9015-2a6320b3f8fe",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students interview their partner using their bias- checked questions and record the answers.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Make sure students are writing down actual numeric answers, not just impressions."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cf4fa80a-ad93-42da-9015-2a6320b3f8fe",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "512da83a-8435-4b8d-ade6-353e79ecc018",
      "position": 14,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students turn a real interview into a concrete plan using someone else's real answers instead of invented placeholder data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 30, Level 1 to work through Steps 1–4 using their partner's real interview answers, then save to their Backpack.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask guiding questions such as:\n- \"What number did your partner actually give you, and does your plan use it meaningfully?\"\n- \"Does your plan reflect what your partner said mattered to them, or what you assumed mattered?\"",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Plan Your Program",
        "progression_name": "Plan Your Program",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this level to check whether students can name a topic with real numeric inputs, describe who it's for and why, and sketch a scene structure that matches their planned data."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "512da83a-8435-4b8d-ade6-353e79ecc018",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8627fee9-6f23-4eeb-927a-bba5e9dcd144",
      "position": 15,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8627fee9-6f23-4eeb-927a-bba5e9dcd144",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
