    {
      "key": "a768b525-3f25-4a6f-af76-0c72f2595417",
      "position": 16,
      "properties": {
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Wrap Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a768b525-3f25-4a6f-af76-0c72f2595417",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e5c4ba13-8998-4df9-8479-8f19689d86c9",
      "position": 17,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What's one question you asked in your interview, and why did you think it would get a meaningful number?*\n- *Did the bias check change anything about your questions or your plan? What did you change, or why not?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students explain the numeric reasoning behind a specific interview question, not just naming a topic, and give a concrete example of what they revised after the bias check, or a specific reason nothing needed to change, not just \"no.\""
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e5c4ba13-8998-4df9-8479-8f19689d86c9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0256a66f-744c-45f1-a740-58b63914fdc9"
      }
    },
