    {
      "key": "c931e0e0-6699-4e42-9d07-a2237369412f",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the milestone structure of the project. Explain that the Wrapped Project is divided into three milestones. Use the visual roadmap to preview the journey students will take: interviewing a real user and planning on Day 1, building their program and animated recap with AI support on Day 2, then testing, fixing, and reflecting on Day 3.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that milestones help them manage time and track progress, just like in real design and development projects. Encourage them to think of each milestone as a \"checkpoint\" to reflect on what's working, what needs improvement, and how their design aligns with their user and purpose."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c931e0e0-6699-4e42-9d07-a2237369412f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "62ef9637-fb14-4cbf-bdc7-b1c0c8660b71"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8b2038cb-f1eb-4cdf-a1f6-b23d069f6ebf",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students turn their Level 1 plan into real, working code, bring that code into a Theater template using AI Tutor to generate the scene cards, then document what they asked AI Tutor for and why they made the design choices they did.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 30, Levels 2–4.\n- **Level 2:** Collect input and calculate at least two meaningful values.\n- **Level 3:** Choose a template and use AI Tutor to build the scene cards.\n- **Level 4:** Document your AI Tutor use and design choices.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask guiding questions such as:\n- \"Which line in your code does which calculation?\"\n- \"Does this scene card actually show your partner's real number?\"",
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Set It Up and Build Your Own",
        "progression_name": "Set It Up and Build Your Own",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this activity to check whether students can compute at least one genuinely meaningful calculation, get real data displaying correctly in a template, and explain what they asked AI Tutor for versus what they did themselves."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8b2038cb-f1eb-4cdf-a1f6-b23d069f6ebf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "62ef9637-fb14-4cbf-bdc7-b1c0c8660b71"
      }
    },
