    {
      "key": "e63c1053-9bba-4c42-860f-e2ffc89a9ce5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Warm Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e63c1053-9bba-4c42-860f-e2ffc89a9ce5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "242570e4-d6b9-40a3-b117-97721c71c98e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students shift from thinking about their program as its creator to anticipating how it might fail for someone who didn't build it.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What's one thing about your program you're not sure will hold up once someone else uses it?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students recognize that they, as the creator, know what's \"supposed\" to happen, but a real user only sees what actually happens. This builds the habit of testing with a real person instead of just testing in your own head."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "242570e4-d6b9-40a3-b117-97721c71c98e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f253285d-d872-4192-90af-227a0282eb7a",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f253285d-d872-4192-90af-227a0282eb7a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e44fff7c-dc5c-4cf5-9b72-2d7cb5f9c9c8",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Activity"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e44fff7c-dc5c-4cf5-9b72-2d7cb5f9c9c8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "79ddce60-3a55-4213-9e2e-60d329e6f4ee",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the project goals."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "79ddce60-3a55-4213-9e2e-60d329e6f4ee",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7ae1f8e3-294c-45a7-8a58-96ca9fdec0d1",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the milestone structure of the project. Explain that the Wrapped Project is divided into three milestones. Use the visual roadmap to preview the journey students will take: interviewing a real user and planning on Day 1, building their program and animated recap with AI support on Day 2, then testing, fixing, and reflecting on Day 3.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that milestones help them manage time and track progress, just like in real design and development projects. Encourage them to think of each milestone as a \"checkpoint\" to reflect on what's working, what needs improvement, and how their design aligns with their user and purpose."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7ae1f8e3-294c-45a7-8a58-96ca9fdec0d1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a7282e92-45a5-43e3-9173-e1239d034d70",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students test functionality across a range of conditions by deliberately trying to break a partner's program, using AI Tutor to help generate inputs they might not have thought of themselves.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Level 3 to run their program, swap with a partner, and use AI Tutor to generate break-it test inputs for their partner's program.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Watch for students testing with only \"normal\" inputs and push them toward genuinely unexpected ones (words where a number's expected, blank input, extreme values).",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Peer Review",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students may be at different points in finishing their program — that's fine, this works even on an unfinished recap. The point is surfacing problems now, not judging completeness."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a7282e92-45a5-43e3-9173-e1239d034d70",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "766673f2-2b2e-4f22-aae0-59a73269adbd",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the TAG Peer Review process and model what thoughtful feedback looks like. Have students pair up or form small groups and TAG one to two peers' projects. They can leave feedback on sticky notes (digital or paper) directly at their peer's workspace or comment within the project rubric if using shared docs.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students may be at different points when it's time for peer review. Reassure them that work doesn't need to be complete to be reviewed — feedback during the process helps improve the final product. Reinforce the mindset that design and development are iterative, and peer feedback offers new perspectives and guidance. If time allows, invite a few students to share one piece of feedback they received that will guide their next steps."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "766673f2-2b2e-4f22-aae0-59a73269adbd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "53190cd0-4ec8-4ff1-a748-66ae91a0063a",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students iteratively improve their program using real feedback from break-it testing and their partner's Tell/Ask/Give, then reflect on the development process as a whole from planning through testing.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 30, Levels 5-6.\n- **Level 5:** Fix what testing surfaced, using AI Tutor as needed.\n- **Level 6:** Answer the Check For Understanding questions.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask guiding questions such as:\n- \"What did your partner's testing find, and did you fix it?\"\n- \"Does your program still match your Level 1 plan, or did something change along the way?\"",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Finish Your Wrapped Program",
        "progression_name": "Finish Your Wrapped Program"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "53190cd0-4ec8-4ff1-a748-66ae91a0063a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3229fed6-aaaf-436a-81f0-742eae0eef7e",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Wrap Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3229fed6-aaaf-436a-81f0-742eae0eef7e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2db3fc4e-9d31-4a7b-911f-7a0ce39699d2",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2db3fc4e-9d31-4a7b-911f-7a0ce39699d2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "071be31f-4490-4e61-b33d-d0f5ac92d9e8",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day and give students a moment to just think about what they learned today."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "071be31f-4490-4e61-b33d-d0f5ac92d9e8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "744bb7b8-1212-4a62-9b58-d2c7f9f43540"
      }
    }
  ],
